Recommends: homelab-agent
Description: Pull fleet TLS certificates from the certificate store
 The consumer half of the fleet certificate pipeline. Fetches this host's
 certificates from homelab-api's store, decrypts them locally with the shared
 key-encryption-key (the API only ever serves ciphertext), validates them,
 installs them atomically and reloads the consuming service -- but only when
 the published certificate actually differs from what is already on disk.
 .
 Runs at boot, ordered BEFORE nginx/postfix/dovecot, so a host that has been
 powered off for weeks serves a current certificate from its first connection
 rather than an expired one until a timer fires; and hourly thereafter for
 renewals that land while the host is up.
 .
 Deliberately fail-safe: an unreachable API, an empty response or a failed
 validation is a logged no-op, never a reason to stop a service from starting.
 An expired local certificate that could not be refreshed is logged loudly so
 it surfaces in fleet status rather than being discovered by a user.
